			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] 2D-animated, Japanese anime style reminiscent of Makoto Shinkai's \"Your Name\", a wide establishing shot frames a long outdoor stone staircase carved into a quiet hillside town at golden hour. A soft orange-to-violet sunset sky with layered wispy clouds stretches overhead, and faint light particles drift through the air. On the upper landing stands a teenage boy with short messy dark hair and a dark gakuran-style school uniform, hands at his sides; several steps below him, on a lower flight, stands a teenage girl with long flowing black hair and a sailor-style uniform, one hand resting on the railing. They face each other across the staircase and their eyes meet. The camera holds a static shot as a gentle wind lifts their hair and the hems of their uniforms and a few fallen leaves spiral downward between them. [Shot 2] At 00:04.000, the camera cuts to a medium close-up from the girl's low vantage point, looking up the steps toward the boy. The boy's expression softens as he looks down at her; his hair sways in the wind and warm sunlight catches the edge of his face. [Shot 3] At 00:08.000, the shot cuts to a reverse medium close-up over the boy's shoulder, framing the girl from above as she tilts her head slightly and blinks, her long hair lifting across her cheek. She lifts her free hand a little, as if about to say something, then lets it settle. [Shot 4] At 00:11.500, the camera cuts back to the original wide staircase framing; the camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed, drawing the two figures closer within the composition as the wind swells, light particles bloom around them, and the sunset deepens into rose-pink. They remain locked in a quiet gaze until the end of the shot.\noverall_soundscape: A steady warm wind moves through the staircase with soft rustling of clothing and hair, accompanied by faint distant cicadas and low town ambience. A few dry leaves scrape gently against the stone steps and a distant wind chime rings once.\nnon_diegetic_music: A gentle piano arpeggio at a slow tempo enters first, joined by sustained strings that swell softly beneath, building a simple memorable melody line that rises and gently fades toward the end.",
